IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc24-attendance`

-- ccc24-tests-attendance.l4 -- tests for ccc24-attendance.l4 (Criminal Code ss 697 to 708.1).
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the section, row by row, before the run.  T = JUST TRUE, F = JUST FALSE, N = NOTHING.

§ `Sections 697 to 700.1`

-- 697: arguments are (section 527 applies, a person is required to attend to give evidence in a proceeding to which the Act applies).
#ASSERT `s 697 Part XXII applies` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 697 Part XXII applies` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Except where section 527 applies"
#ASSERT `s 697 Part XXII applies` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 697 Part XXII applies` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 698(1) a subpoena may be issued in accordance with Part XXII requiring the person to attend to give evidence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 698(1) a subpoena may be issued in accordance with Part XXII requiring the person to attend to give evidence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Where a person is likely to give material evidence"
-- 698(2): arguments are (likely to give material evidence, will not attend, evading service, the issuer has power to issue a subpoena).
#ASSERT `s 698(2) a court, justice or provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 17 to cause the person to be arrested and to be brought to give evidence` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 698(2) a court, justice or provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 17 to cause the person to be arrested and to be brought to give evidence` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 698(2) a court, justice or provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 17 to cause the person to be arrested and to be brought to give evidence` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- nothing made to appear
#ASSERT `s 698(2) a court, justice or provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 17 to cause the person to be arrested and to be brought to give evidence` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not likely to give material evidence
#ASSERT `s 698(2) a court, justice or provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 17 to cause the person to be arrested and to be brought to give evidence` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the issuer has no power to issue a subpoena
-- 698(3): arguments are (paragraph (2)(a) applies, a subpoena has first been issued, a warrant in Form 17 is to be issued).
#ASSERT `s 698(3) the bar on issuing a warrant in Form 17 applies` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- no subpoena first, (2)(a) does not apply
#ASSERT `s 698(3) the bar on issuing a warrant in Form 17 applies` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless a subpoena has first been issued"
#ASSERT `s 698(3) the bar on issuing a warrant in Form 17 applies` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Except where paragraph (2)(a) applies"
#ASSERT `s 698(3) the bar on issuing a warrant in Form 17 applies` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 699(1) the subpoena shall be issued out of the court before which the attendance of the person is required` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 699(1) the subpoena shall be issued out of the court before which the attendance of the person is required` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

`ccc24 fixture 699a` MEANS `s 699(2)(a) a provincial court judge or a justice`
`ccc24 fixture 699b` MEANS `s 699(2)(b) a provincial court judge or a superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province in which the proceedings were instituted`
`ccc24 fixture 699x` MEANS `s 699(2) another issuer`

-- 699(2): arguments are (the issuer, the proceeding is one of those the subsection names, the person is within the province).
#ASSERT `s 699(2) the subpoena shall be issued by the issuer` `ccc24 fixture 699a` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 699(2) the subpoena shall be issued by the issuer` `ccc24 fixture 699a` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a) is for a person within the province
#ASSERT `s 699(2) the subpoena shall be issued by the issuer` `ccc24 fixture 699b` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 699(2) the subpoena shall be issued by the issuer` `ccc24 fixture 699b` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b) is for a person not within the province
#ASSERT `s 699(2) the subpoena shall be issued by the issuer` `ccc24 fixture 699x` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 699(2) the subpoena shall be issued by the issuer` `ccc24 fixture 699a` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a proceeding the subsection does not name
#ASSERT `s 699(3) the bar on issuing a subpoena out of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction pursuant to paragraph (2)(b) applies` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 699(3) the bar on issuing a subpoena out of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction pursuant to paragraph (2)(b) applies` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "except pursuant to an order of a judge"
#ASSERT `s 699(3) the bar on issuing a subpoena out of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction pursuant to paragraph (2)(b) applies` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 699(4) the subpoena or warrant is under the seal of the court and is signed by a judge of the court or by the clerk of the court` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 699(4) the subpoena or warrant is under the seal of the court and is signed by a judge of the court or by the clerk of the court` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 699(4) the subpoena or warrant is under the seal of the court and is signed by a judge of the court or by the clerk of the court` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 699(4) the subpoena or warrant is under the seal of the court and is signed by a judge of the court or by the clerk of the court` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 699(5) the subpoena or warrant is signed by the justice, provincial court judge or the clerk of the court` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 699(5) the subpoena or warrant is signed by the justice, provincial court judge or the clerk of the court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 699(5) the subpoena or warrant is signed by the justice, provincial court judge or the clerk of the court` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 699(5.1) the subpoena is issued by a judge and signed by the judge or the clerk of the court` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 699(5.1) the subpoena is issued by a judge and signed by the judge or the clerk of the court` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- issued by a justice, not a judge
#ASSERT `s 699(5.1) the subpoena is issued by a judge and signed by the judge or the clerk of the court` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 699(5.1) the subpoena is issued by a judge and signed by the judge or the clerk of the court` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 699(6) the subpoena may be in Form 16` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 699(6) the subpoena may be in Form 16` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the (7) case is Form 16.1
#ASSERT `s 699(6) the subpoena may be in Form 16` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 699(7) the subpoena is in Form 16.1` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 699(7) the subpoena is in Form 16.1` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 699(7) the subpoena is in Form 16.1` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 699(7) the subpoena is in Form 16.1` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 700(1) the subpoena requires the person to attend, at a time and place stated in the subpoena, to give evidence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 700(1) the subpoena requires the person to attend, at a time and place stated in the subpoena, to give evidence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 700(1) the subpoena requires the person to attend, at a time and place stated in the subpoena, to give evidence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 700(2) the person must attend and remain in attendance throughout the proceedings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 700(2) the person must attend and remain in attendance throughout the proceedings` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless he is excused"
#ASSERT `s 700(2) the person must attend and remain in attendance throughout the proceedings` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not served with a subpoena
#ASSERT `s 700.1(1) a subpoena shall be issued out of the court to order the person to give the evidence at that place` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 700.1(1) a subpoena shall be issued out of the court to order the person to give the evidence at that place` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the technology is not available
#ASSERT `s 700.1(1) a subpoena shall be issued out of the court to order the person to give the evidence at that place` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 700.1(1) a subpoena shall be issued out of the court to order the person to give the evidence at that place` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 700.1(2) the section applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the subpoena issued under section 700.1` 699 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 700.1(2) the section applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the subpoena issued under section 700.1` 700 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 700.1(2) the section applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the subpoena issued under section 700.1` 701 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 700.1(2) the section applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the subpoena issued under section 700.1` 702 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 700.1(2) the section applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the subpoena issued under section 700.1` 703.2 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 700.1(2) the section applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the subpoena issued under section 700.1` 703.1 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 700.1(2) the section applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the subpoena issued under section 700.1` 704 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- outside the list
#ASSERT `s 700.1(2) the section applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the subpoena issued under section 700.1` 698 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 700.1(2) the section applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the subpoena issued under section 700.1` 700 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Sections 701 to 703.2`

#ASSERT `s 701(1) the subpoena shall be served in a province by the server` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 701(1) the subpoena shall be served in a province by the server` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 701(1) the subpoena shall be served in a province by the server` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 701(2) the subpoena has been served personally on the person to whom it is directed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 701(2) the subpoena has been served personally on the person to whom it is directed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 701(2) the subpoena has been served personally on the person to whom it is directed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 701.1 service of a document may be made in accordance with the laws of the province relating to offences created by the laws of that province` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 701.1 service of a document may be made in accordance with the laws of the province relating to offences created by the laws of that province` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 702(1) the subpoena has effect anywhere in Canada according to its terms` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 702(1) the subpoena has effect anywhere in Canada according to its terms` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 702(2) the subpoena has effect anywhere in the province in which it is issued` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 702(2) the subpoena has effect anywhere in the province in which it is issued` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 703(1) the warrant of arrest or committal may be executed anywhere in Canada` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 703(1) the warrant of arrest or committal may be executed anywhere in Canada` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 703(2) the warrant of arrest or committal may be executed anywhere in the province in which it is issued` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 703(2) the warrant of arrest or committal may be executed anywhere in the province in which it is issued` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 703.1 a summons may be served anywhere in Canada and, if served, is effective notwithstanding the territorial jurisdiction of the authority that issued the summons` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 703.1 a summons may be served anywhere in Canada and, if served, is effective notwithstanding the territorial jurisdiction of the authority that issued the summons` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

`ccc24 fixture 7032a` MEANS `s 703.2(a) a municipality`
`ccc24 fixture 7032b` MEANS `s 703.2(b) an organization other than a municipality`

-- 703.2: arguments are (the kind, process is to be or may be served, no other method is provided, delivered to a municipal officer, delivered to an officer of another organization).
#ASSERT `s 703.2 service may be effected by delivery to the officer` `ccc24 fixture 7032a` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 703.2 service may be effected by delivery to the officer` `ccc24 fixture 7032a` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- delivered to someone the paragraph does not name
#ASSERT `s 703.2 service may be effected by delivery to the officer` `ccc24 fixture 7032b` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 703.2 service may be effected by delivery to the officer` `ccc24 fixture 7032b` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 703.2 service may be effected by delivery to the officer` `ccc24 fixture 7032a` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "and no other method of service is provided"
#ASSERT `s 703.2 service may be effected by delivery to the officer` `ccc24 fixture 7032b` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Sections 704 to 707`

#ASSERT `s 704(1) the justice may issue a warrant in Form 18 directing a peace officer to arrest the person and to bring the person before the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom the person is bound to appear` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 704(1) the justice may issue a warrant in Form 18 directing a peace officer to arrest the person and to bring the person before the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom the person is bound to appear` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the justice is not satisfied
#ASSERT `s 704(1) the justice may issue a warrant in Form 18 directing a peace officer to arrest the person and to bring the person before the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom the person is bound to appear` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Where a person is bound by recognizance"
#ASSERT `s 704(2) section 528 applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to the warrant` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 704(2) section 528 applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to the warrant` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 704(3) the person is entitled to receive a copy of the information on which the warrant for the arrest was issued` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 704(3) the person is entitled to receive a copy of the information on which the warrant for the arrest was issued` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "on request"
#ASSERT `s 704(3) the person is entitled to receive a copy of the information on which the warrant for the arrest was issued` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 705(1) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom the person was required to attend may issue a warrant in Form 17 for the arrest of the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 705(1) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom the person was required to attend may issue a warrant in Form 17 for the arrest of the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not established that the person is likely to give material evidence
#ASSERT `s 705(1) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom the person was required to attend may issue a warrant in Form 17 for the arrest of the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not established that the subpoena was served in accordance with Part XXII
#ASSERT `s 705(1) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom the person was required to attend may issue a warrant in Form 17 for the arrest of the person` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the person attended and remained
#ASSERT `s 705(1) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom the person was required to attend may issue a warrant in Form 17 for the arrest of the person` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 705(2) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom the person was bound to attend may issue a warrant in Form 17 for the arrest of the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 705(2) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom the person was bound to attend may issue a warrant in Form 17 for the arrest of the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 705(2) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom the person was bound to attend may issue a warrant in Form 17 for the arrest of the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 705(3) the warrant may be executed anywhere in Canada` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 705(3) the warrant may be executed anywhere in Canada` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 705(4) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge may, by an endorsement on the warrant in Form 29.1, authorize the release of the person on an undertaking with conditions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 705(4) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge may, by an endorsement on the warrant in Form 29.1, authorize the release of the person on an undertaking with conditions` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 705(5) the endorsing court, judge, justice or provincial court judge must include the conditions of the undertaking that it considers necessary to ensure that the person will appear and give evidence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 705(5) the endorsing court, judge, justice or provincial court judge must include the conditions of the undertaking that it considers necessary to ensure that the person will appear and give evidence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 705(5) the endorsing court, judge, justice or provincial court judge must include the conditions of the undertaking that it considers necessary to ensure that the person will appear and give evidence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 705(6) the person may apply to the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge to vary the undertaking` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 705(6) the person may apply to the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge to vary the undertaking` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 705(6) the person may apply to the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge to vary the undertaking` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 705(7) the undertaking is deemed to be an undertaking given under section 705.1` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 705(7) the undertaking is deemed to be an undertaking given under section 705.1` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 705.1(1) a peace officer may release the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 705.1(1) a peace officer may release the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no undertaking in Form 10.1
#ASSERT `s 705.1(1) a peace officer may release the person` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the warrant is not endorsed
#ASSERT `s 705.1(1) a peace officer may release the person` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 705.1(2) the undertaking sets out the name, date of birth and contact information of the person and information about the proceeding` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 705.1(2) the undertaking sets out the name, date of birth and contact information of the person and information about the proceeding` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 705.1(2) the undertaking sets out the name, date of birth and contact information of the person and information about the proceeding` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 705.1(3) the undertaking includes a condition that the person attend court at the time and place stated in the undertaking and attend afterwards as required by the court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 705.1(3) the undertaking includes a condition that the person attend court at the time and place stated in the undertaking and attend afterwards as required by the court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 705.1(4) the undertaking includes the condition imposed by the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge under subsection 705(5) and set out in the endorsement made in Form 29.1` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 705.1(4) the undertaking includes the condition imposed by the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge under subsection 705(5) and set out in the endorsement made in Form 29.1` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 705.1(4) the undertaking includes the condition imposed by the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge under subsection 705(5) and set out in the endorsement made in Form 29.1` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 705.1(5) the person has been requested to sign the undertaking in duplicate and one of the duplicates has been given to them` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 705.1(5) the person has been requested to sign the undertaking in duplicate and one of the duplicates has been given to them` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 705.1(5) the person has been requested to sign the undertaking in duplicate and one of the duplicates has been given to them` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 705.1(6) the lack of the person's signature invalidates the undertaking` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "does not invalidate"
#ASSERT `s 705.1(6) the lack of the person's signature invalidates the undertaking` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 705.1(7): arguments are (an undertaking was given, the conditions were cancelled, changed, the person appeared and remained in attendance).
#ASSERT `s 705.1(7) the conditions with respect to the undertaking remain in effect` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 705.1(7) the conditions with respect to the undertaking remain in effect` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- cancelled
#ASSERT `s 705.1(7) the conditions with respect to the undertaking remain in effect` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- changed
#ASSERT `s 705.1(7) the conditions with respect to the undertaking remain in effect` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the person appeared and remained
#ASSERT `s 705.1(7) the conditions with respect to the undertaking remain in effect` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

`ccc24 fixture 706a` MEANS `s 706 order that the person be detained in custody`
`ccc24 fixture 706b` MEANS `s 706 order that the person be released on recognizance with sureties`
`ccc24 fixture 706c` MEANS `s 706 order that the person be released on recognizance without sureties`
`ccc24 fixture 706x` MEANS `s 706 another order`

#ASSERT `s 706 the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice may make the order` `ccc24 fixture 706a` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 706 the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice may make the order` `ccc24 fixture 706b` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 706 the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice may make the order` `ccc24 fixture 706c` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 706 the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice may make the order` `ccc24 fixture 706x` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 706 the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice may make the order` `ccc24 fixture 706a` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not brought before the court under such a warrant
#ASSERT `s 706 the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice may make the order` `ccc24 fixture 706a` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not made so that the person will appear and give evidence

-- 707(1): arguments are (detained for the purpose only of giving evidence, the number of days, brought before a judge in time).
#ASSERT `s 707(1) the bar on detaining a witness for more than thirty days applies` TRUE 31 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 707(1) the bar on detaining a witness for more than thirty days applies` TRUE 30 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a period the text fixes: the thirtieth day is within it
#ASSERT `s 707(1) the bar on detaining a witness for more than thirty days applies` TRUE 90 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- brought before the judge in time ("unless")
#ASSERT `s 707(1) the bar on detaining a witness for more than thirty days applies` FALSE 40 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- detained for another purpose too
#ASSERT `s 707(2) the judge must fix a time before the expiration of the thirty days for the hearing of the application and cause notice of it to be given, and the person having custody of the witness must cause the witness to be brought before a judge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 707(2) the judge must fix a time before the expiration of the thirty days for the hearing of the application and cause notice of it to be given, and the person having custody of the witness must cause the witness to be brought before a judge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 707(2) the judge must fix a time before the expiration of the thirty days for the hearing of the application and cause notice of it to be given, and the person having custody of the witness must cause the witness to be brought before a judge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 707(3) first sentence: arguments are (brought before a judge, the judge is not satisfied that continued detention is justified).
#ASSERT `s 707(3) the judge must order the witness to be discharged or to be released on recognizance, with or without sureties` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 707(3) the judge must order the witness to be discharged or to be released on recognizance, with or without sureties` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 707(3) the judge must order the witness to be discharged or to be released on recognizance, with or without sureties` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 707(3) continued detention: arguments are (brought before a judge, the judge is satisfied, total days, an until-event has happened).
#ASSERT `s 707(3) the judge may order the continued detention of the witness` TRUE TRUE 60 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 707(3) the judge may order the continued detention of the witness` TRUE TRUE 90 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the ninetieth day is within the limit
#ASSERT `s 707(3) the judge may order the continued detention of the witness` TRUE TRUE 91 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "shall not in any case exceed 90 days"
#ASSERT `s 707(3) the judge may order the continued detention of the witness` TRUE TRUE 60 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "until they do what is required"
#ASSERT `s 707(3) the judge may order the continued detention of the witness` TRUE FALSE 60 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the judge is not satisfied: "if the judge is satisfied"
#ASSERT `s 707(3) the judge may order the continued detention of the witness` FALSE TRUE 60 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Sections 708 and 708.1`

-- 708(1): arguments are (required by law to attend or remain, fails to attend or remain, has a lawful excuse).
#ASSERT `s 708(1) the person is guilty of contempt of court` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 708(1) the person is guilty of contempt of court` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "without lawful excuse" limits the offence in its own wording
#ASSERT `s 708(1) the person is guilty of contempt of court` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 708(1) the person is guilty of contempt of court` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 708(2) a court, judge, justice or provincial court judge may deal summarily with the person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 708(2) a court, judge, justice or provincial court judge may deal summarily with the person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 708(2) the greatest fine the person is liable to` TRUE EQUALS JUST (`a fine of` 5000)
#ASSERT `s 708(2) the greatest fine the person is liable to` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 708(2) the longest imprisonment the person is liable to` TRUE EQUALS JUST (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`)
#ASSERT `s 708(2) the longest imprisonment the person is liable to` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 708(2) the person may be ordered to pay the costs that are incident to the service of any process under Part XXII and to the person's detention, if any` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 708(2) the person may be ordered to pay the costs that are incident to the service of any process under Part XXII and to the person's detention, if any` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 708(2) the person may be ordered to pay the costs that are incident to the service of any process under Part XXII and to the person's detention, if any` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 708(3) a conviction under section 708 may be in Form 38` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 708(3) a conviction under section 708 may be in Form 38` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 708(3) a warrant of committal in respect of a conviction under section 708 may be in Form 25` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 708(3) a warrant of committal in respect of a conviction under section 708 may be in Form 25` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 708.1 the copy has the same probative force as the original for the purposes of the Criminal Code` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 708.1 the copy has the same probative force as the original for the purposes of the Criminal Code` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 708.1 the copy has the same probative force as the original for the purposes of the Criminal Code` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
